{"kind":"request","text":"Review J4's live witness outcome against the done-when rows of parent 0c3091fa. Return one verdict on whether the witness closes those rows. The planner deploys main after your verdict (its act f7f82d51).\n\nThe planner ran every command once, on Worker da13242c and Source 112eff12, with no halt. I read the public receipts and results, and I released each later phase with the previous phase's state digest. I read nothing private.\n\n## Evidence\n\nThe unit is /Users/hughpyle/play/artroom-evidence/2026-10-31-j4-live-outcome: 162 files, 2,218,413 bytes, read-only. SHA256SUMS digest fdbcf91dac0c225b1f4651212f92853f777832003282babac44f0f18c055dcca. The manifest beside the directory has digest 4a60e39979c7f781597ea3fe90e36c64081133b42a39407fb3d8971dda89fc9d. I reran SHA256SUMS and it is clean.\n\nThe unit holds each capture's records and public result, the four channel captures, and the channel inputs and scripts. It holds one copy of each packet's source, because all six later captures have the same packet source by tree digest. It keeps no runtime Source copy, because each capture's source-index.json binds those bytes. A scan for token shapes found nothing. phases.json has one row per phase, read from the receipts.\n\n| Phase | Word | Receipt | Result | State | Requests |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| setup | setup-complete | 472ddacb | c99c942d | 292e2636 | 106 |\n| rehold | rehold-complete | 0e0bd013 | 4d6925cf | a17ae935 | 43 |\n| work | work-complete | fc4c5346 | 0150f252 | ad15c8bd | 82 |\n| manifest | manifest-complete | e7d49f42 | e341191d | 571e0b16 | 27 |\n| review | review-complete | 86261fbe | 03b7ce3e | 731bcfe4 | 17 |\n| publish | publish-complete, acceptanceClaim true | 71d92504 | 81ad18b6 | fb1b8082 | 24 |\n| cleanup | cleanup-complete | 1f4d8f25 | 6a82e3c5 | 89e929d1 | 20 |\n\nEvery phase closed with exit 0, capture 0 and no timeout. Each later phase's parent equals the previous phase's state. I read the six later stderr.log files, and each holds only the known DEP0205 warning. I did not reread setup's stderr.log for this report.\n\n## The rows of 0c3091fa\n\n**Two agents each push to their own hold's fork: met.** Token 5 pushed commit 880b6007 to fork 23-24-1, and token 6 pushed commit 402f376c to fork 28-29-1. Each fork's receive-pack POST answered 200. Each credential handoff answered 403 to the wrong key, 200 to the owner, and 403 to a repeat. Each token was refused on the other fork and on the room, 403 at receive-pack discovery, so no pack went out.\n\n**A token stops working when its hold ends: met at the provider for token 5, and only in native records for token 6.**\n- Token 5, hold 23. The release act is lane seq 37 and the revoke outcome is seq 38. The token's receive-pack discovery answered 200 at 23:00:53.631 UTC. A push with the old token answered 403 at 23:00:58.276, 14 min 50 s before the token's stated end.\n- Controls. The independent read token read the same fork with 200 before and after the refusal, at 880b6007 with the probe ref absent. Token 6 wrote a new ref at 23:00:58.673, after hold 23 ended, so the provider had not stopped all writes.\n- The result's own qualification applies: this shows the old token stopped and does not show why. The probe tried a write only. Nothing read with the old token after the end.\n- Token 6, hold 28. The release act is lane seq 53, and native shows the token ended with a confirmed revoke. No provider probe ran. The stated end, 23:15:49, has passed, so no later read can separate revocation from expiry.\n\n**The change publishes from the chosen fork: met.** The manifest at lane seq 46 names commit 402f376c, tree 2a0159cc. The review is seq 47 and the merge is seq 48, with merge state published. Publication 10 binds that manifest and commit, and written receipt 13 names the commit. Destination's branch head equals the commit. A provider read of the room's branch with the room read token equals the commit. That comparison covers the ref only. No fresh clone compared the published bytes.\n\n**On the deployment: met.** Health and version read da13242c in every phase. The link from that version to Source 112eff12 stays the reviewed operator attestation.\n\nThe parent's source conditions closed at landing 5dc9765f, receipt d156cef5, approval 7710ed11. I did not recheck its \"not before\" order for this report.\n\n## Limits\n\n- \"Agents\" here means two members of kind agent and role agent, whose keys one operator script used. No hosted agent engine ran, and native Task and export stay out of scope.\n- The holds ended two ways. Holds 23 and 28 ended by release. Holds 9 and 16 ended by time, and native shows their setup tokens revoked with confirmed outcomes. No provider read covers a timed end.\n- This is one run on one provider result set. ownerMayReview:true is the scratch-room policy for this witness.\n- The independent read token's read scope rests on the planner's attestation that it minted the token read. The planner revoked it by ID, and a read answered 403 at 23:03:04.601, before its expiry. The Wrangler child exits 143 on the channel's SIGTERM in both mint-read and revoke-read.\n- The record ends at each phase's last read, and native keeps running after that. Cleanup's last recorded fact is lane seq 53.\n\n## What your reviews said the report must state\n\n- Routes. Rows L06 to L29 had no proof under this Worker, apart from L08. Each row that a closed step uses has now run once. The public results list Git requests one by one and only count the rest, so a closed step is the evidence for a non-Git route. L30 ran through the planner's channel. L31 (deletion) and L32 (Register) did not run.\n- Setup's R28, R29 and R30 had no proof under any Worker. They have now run once, by setup-complete.\n- Your unknowns from 0d1717a5 now have answers for this run: both second forks came from seed 29c702da on attempt 1, and each denial probe answered 403. A provider read confirms only token 5's revoke and the 